%abc-2.1
% CONTROL — %%keywarn, which appears in abcjs's own tests and in NEITHER corpus. It stops a
% mid-tune K: being DRAWN without stopping it taking effect, and it takes the INTEGER 0 or
% 1: `%%keywarn false` is an error and is dropped, so tune 3 must be byte-identical to
% tune 1. Goldens generated by running abcjs 6.7.0 at {staffwidth: 670}.
X:1
T:keywarn absent
L:1/4
M:4/4
K:C
CDEF|
K:G
GAB^c|

X:2
T:keywarn 0
L:1/4
M:4/4
%%keywarn 0
K:C
CDEF|
K:G
GAB^c|

X:3
T:keywarn false is a no-op
L:1/4
M:4/4
%%keywarn false
K:C
CDEF|
K:G
GAB^c|
